## Identify Files for Synchronization

xCAT includes functionality to synchronize files from the head node to managed
hosts via *synclists*. This is one way to distribute user credentials to compute
nodes.
{%- if is_xcat_stateless %} The synclist is applied when the compute image
boots.{% else %} The default `syncfiles` postscript applies the synclist during
the install, and changes can be pushed on demand afterwards with
`updatenode`.{% endif %} Enable the synclist feature and register credential
files:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Import files -->
```bash
# Synclists are registered per image type
xcat_synclist_dir="/install/custom/{{ xcat_image_type }}"

# Define path for xCAT synclist file
mkdir -p ${xcat_synclist_dir}
chdef -t osimage -o ${xcat_osimage} \
    synclists="${xcat_synclist_dir}/compute.synclist"

# Add credential files to synclist
echo "/etc/passwd  -> /etc/passwd"  >  ${xcat_synclist_dir}/compute.synclist
echo "/etc/group   -> /etc/group"   >> ${xcat_synclist_dir}/compute.synclist
echo "/etc/shadow  -> /etc/shadow"  >> ${xcat_synclist_dir}/compute.synclist
echo "/etc/munge/munge.key -> /etc/munge/munge.key" \
    >> ${xcat_synclist_dir}/compute.synclist
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

The `updatenode compute -F` command distributes changes made to any defined
synchronization files. Use the uppercase `-F` flag; lowercase `-f` targets
service nodes.
